  "worked_solution": "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{y}={\u222c}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is a type II plane region, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073832/assets/6cfa58d15b2a1f05aa4d4d088d44b44d6b3225084f627bc8078617d85d801957.png)\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le y,\\,1\\le y\\le 2}\n$$\n\nand $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{y}{x}.$ \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{y} & ={\u222c}_{D}x\\cdot \\frac{y}{x}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\u222c}_{D}y\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{y}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}y[{\\int }_{1}^{y}\\text{d}x]\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}y[x]_{x=1}^{x=y}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}y(y-1)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{y}^{2}-y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{y=1}^{y=2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{8}{3}-2)-(\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
